      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p9_s1"
      },
      "text": "McpRoXy.exe SoundMax.dll These strings were all observed and highlighted by Bit9 here .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_31",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Operation_EphemeralHydra",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p9_s2"
      },
      "text": "As Bit9 notes in their blog, Trojan.APT.9002 (aka Hydraq/McRAT) was also used in the original Operation Aurora campaign, and the “rat_UnInstall” string can be found in the original Aurora samples confirming the lineage.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
